WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
And as I say,

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:12.280
having to play sixty minutes and having to . . . We had no specialists to snap the ball back for long punts,

3
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.880
short punts, or no T-formation.

4
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:26.140
We run from a single wing and you had to get the ball up out of the water and lead the tailbacks as they would take their steps.

5
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:33.580
And then, the rules of the game, if you went out during a quarter you couldn’t come back in until the next quarter.

6
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:40.800
So that’s why most of us had to play . . . especially in close ball games, play the whole ball game.

7
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.620
And up until towards the end of my senior year I was the only center they had.

8
00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.840
It seemed that way, the amount that I played.

9
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.460
Were you a better center or a linebacker?

10
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.880
Well, I was a better both of them. [Purdy laughs]
